                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9f23abb1-0c34-3d68-8426-dcd32a21e382",
                        "entry_id": "e52f7090-081c-3fb2-adc9-fbb09d0afaa6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unreasonably optimistic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1177819-838e-4acb-aa22-e8a7e7795561",
                                "sense_id": "9f23abb1-0c34-3d68-8426-dcd32a21e382",
                                "text": "Accordingly the objection “Is not optimalism simply too Pollyanna-ish to be plausible?” can be met effectively."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d7b4430-3983-4646-8ec7-9d90214134a1",
                                "sense_id": "9f23abb1-0c34-3d68-8426-dcd32a21e382",
                                "text": "Even long before this choice of character of the year was made, critics were complaining about the [Chinese] government’s Pollyannaish touting of mèng 梦, saying that the dreams of most people were in vain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8566cd03-775c-4f7c-8f91-da1e3c000351",
                                "sense_id": "9f23abb1-0c34-3d68-8426-dcd32a21e382",
                                "text": "If that sounds a little bit Pollyannaish, it’s because Schmidhuber’s own experience[…]must have taught him that competition can create losers as well as winners."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f344556-ea64-4502-a303-7515ec7318e4",
                                "sense_id": "9f23abb1-0c34-3d68-8426-dcd32a21e382",
                                "text": "On this basis, Bridle argues, it’s possible to conceive of a new kind of “guardianship” of our frazzled planet and its poisoned wells, one in which we all work together. This seems Pollyanna-ish as much as Panglossian to me […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
